lement or  another  in the end cordelia winds up coming  through as the supreme which after  pitting the girls against each other all  season feels utterly underwhelming  and a little bit like a cop-out having  fun yet  yeah it's a real party even an  appearance by stevie nicks who opens the  episode with a short impromptu music  video  can't save this lukewarm finale which  culminates in fiona finding herself  trapped in her own personal hell  being stuck in an old farmhouse for  eternity with her former lover the  axeman  watching jessica lang frantically scream  about the house's foundations does  elicit some chuckles  but as a whole this ending doesn't do  any service to the roller coaster of a  season that preceded it  when it comes to american horror story  it's not uncommon for a season to  premiere strong  only to start losing steam as plots  become more and more convoluted and  characters come and go  freak show is no exception even though  the season ranks quite low among the  others  monsters among us is a standout episode  in its own right audiences meet elsa  mars played by jessica lang in her final  full season of american horror story  as she rescues conjoined twins bet and  dot from a hospital only to place them  in her freak show  the episode also seamlessly introduces  twisty a terrifying murderous clown as  well as socialite gloria mott and her  deranged son dandy  how's that it's better this seat's warm  mother made it toasty for you gross  anyway to cap it all off elsa performs a  david bowie song  the aptly name life on mars to be  precise to close out the episode and  reveals her own secret she's a double  amputee  the premiere of freak show is an  excellent example of a successful start  it expertly sets up the rest of the  season and despite the lackluster  episodes that follow  it remains one of the standouts of the  entire series  even though it had an extraordinarily  strong start freak show much like its  predecessor coven  ended with a 